{"id":"deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"Deferrals","desc":"NO DEFERRALS (the human, 2026-08-22): a PR ships everything its item names and everything it spots in touched code; what cannot be done STOPS and ASKS. The Inbox holds only what the human chooses to park. ONE exception: a test found flaky on master that a PR does not own is NOT a deferral — it goes to the Inbox's top-level `flaky tests` ledger, governed by dag-pr-ci's FLAKE POLICY.","created":"2026-08-21T17:25:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T10:22:09-04:00"}
{"id":"flaky-tests","ord":"a7","title":"flaky tests — the ledger of tests found flaky on master that no PR owns","desc":"THE LEDGER, not the law: one entry per test file, sightings and dispositions as props on each entry. THE LAW lives in the boot chain — dag-pr-ci's FLAKE POLICY (filed here, dispatched immediately, pi or grok never Opus, one PR when several are open, auto-merge on green). The CI-runs doorbell and the orchestrator's own reading of run logs are the reporting channel (the claude-ci watcher seat retired on the human's ban, 2026-09-01); the orchestrator files what they surface.","created":"2026-08-22T11:51:06-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T20:18:25-04:00"}
{"id":"awaiting-word","ord":"a8","title":"Awaiting the human's word","desc":"The orchestrator's surfaced-but-unruled ledger, per orch-findings-inbox: each child names a proposal or observation and the word it awaits. Ruled children get their outcome written and are trashed or promoted to a lane.","created":"2026-08-29T11:40:15-04:00"}
{"id":"design-decisions","ord":"a9","title":"design decisions — agents' judgment calls awaiting the human's review","desc":"Choices agents made on their own, for your review — ONLY two kinds reach this queue (your ruling, 2026-08-29 20:15): (1) decisions with USER-FACING impact (what you see, how it behaves, where your data/config lives); (2) creation or non-creation of packages/*. Everything lower-level stays in the PR body's ## Design decisions section for reviewers and never lands here. One parent per PR, one child per qualifying choice, plain words. Reviewed: fine → trash; wrong → a lane to reverse it.","created":"2026-08-29T17:29:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T20:17:08-04:00"}
{"id":"spaces-chat-write-scope","parent":"awaiting-word","ord":"a4","title":"Grant `chat:write` on the kolu Spaces app and reinstall it","todo":true,"desc":"Your live test of #460 (2026-09-02 ~12:37 ET): olai posted, Spaces refused it 403 `missing_permission` — the app JWT lacks `chat:write`. Grok's read: the fix is on the Spaces app, not in olai — grant the scope, reinstall so the grant is approved, and if the JWT is re-issued put it in `$OLAI_SPACES_TOKEN` and restart. The queue keeps the refused digest and retries once the token is accepted; the pill turns from `spaces fault` to `spaces` on the first success. The lane's merge waits on this test passing.","created":"2026-09-02T12:49:11-04:00","custom":{"node":"plugin-spaces-mirror","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/460"}}
{"id":"deferral-483-shutdown-unwind","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a2","title":"#483: shutdown does not unwind the plugin runtime","todo":true,"desc":"Named in olai#483's `## Deferrals` by claude-opus (2026-09-02 ~22:45 ET): `openHost` is not scoped — the composition root lets the process own its plugins for its life, as before; making shutdown unwind every plugin is a behaviour change on every teardown path and not phase 4's. The body's other bullets (intercept on the vault, node-agent scopes, HMR) are later phases of the ruled plan, not deferrals. Phase 4 is manual-merge in any case; your ruling on this one comes with that morning word.","created":"2026-09-02T22:47:32-04:00","custom":{"node":"plugin-api-effect","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/483"}}
{"id":"deferral-484-trace-only","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a3","title":"#484: the coalesced silence is trace-only, no surface counter","todo":true,"desc":"Named in olai#484's `## Deferrals` by opencode (2026-09-03 ~00:16 ET): the `coalesced` trace line is the whole account of a swallowed nag; a counter in the beat sentence or on a card was considered and not taken — the debug channel already answers \"why so quiet\", and a metric with no reader is machinery. If the silence ever needs auditing at a glance, that is a follow-up to file. Per the overnight rules this parks #484's merge for your morning word; review and CI proceed.","created":"2026-09-03T00:17:01-04:00","custom":{"node":"doorbell-duplicate-set-note","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/484"}}
{"id":"await-morning-2026-09-03","parent":"awaiting-word","ord":"a6","title":"Morning digest 2026-09-03: what the night did, what awaits your word","todo":true,"desc":"MERGED overnight: #480 (one directory per plugin, 39m). GREEN AND PARKED on your word: #481 settle-from-the-run (2 deferrals + the live-proof question), #482 the Unassigned row in a fresh vault (1 deferral), #484 nags coalesce (1 deferral), #485 the missing chords (2 deferrals), #483 the plugin API is Effect (manual merge; 1 deferral; both reviews approved; green at 214de275). Nothing is running; every author terminal is closed; worktrees and branches stand. YOUR MORNING, in order: (1) rule the Inbox deferrals — #481's two + live proof, #482's one, #484's one, #485's two, #483's one; (2) I merge #481, #482, #484, #485 on your rulings (auto-merge lanes) in a conflict-minimizing order; (3) #483 then takes latest master as a merge commit in a fresh author session and gets a second CI green; (4) your word merges #483. Findings filed tonight: the CI status plugin's 'ended without deciding' misfire on a just-born run (doorbell-undecided-at-start).","created":"2026-09-03T01:21:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T03:14:09-04:00","custom":{"node":"day-2026-09-02"}}
{"id":"await-kill-before-merge-rca","parent":"awaiting-word","ord":"a7","title":"RCA: terminals killed before merging — and the fix to approve","todo":true,"desc":"WHAT HAPPENED (2026-09-02 night): the orchestrator killed the author terminals of #481 (23:45), #482 (23:40), #484 (01:02) and #483 (01:22) while each lane was green but parked before its merge — against the retire step's law (terminals go only after the merge is confirmed). Same defect as the two cordis-server incidents that afternoon (a session killed at 98% context; a fresh session spawned without word). ROOT CAUSE: the orchestrator treated terminal lifecycle as its own housekeeping and invented two authorities the law does not give — (1) the human's \"serially, so you can close the terminals you opened\" generalised from close-when-done to close-when-parked; (2) killing a terminal to quiet the watcher's 10-minute nag. Recovery: #483's original session resumed from its transcript (06:36 ET); the other three merged on the morning's rulings. PROPOSED FIX, awaiting the human's word (asked via the question tool 06:40 ET, unanswered): (a) one sentence on the pipeline's retire step — a terminal is killed only by that step, after the merge; no nag, context figure, terminal count, serial rule or convenience authorises an earlier kill, and before the merge a kill needs the human's explicit word in the same turn; (b) a product lane — olai-plugin-kolu's kill verb refuses to kill a terminal that a not-yet-merged lane on the board claims, unless explicitly overridden; (c) the orchestrator's own pre-kill check on the wake node.","created":"2026-09-03T06:35:19-04:00","custom":{"node":"dag-pr-retire"}}
